# Snyk (https://snyk.io) policy file
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-JS-UUID-16133035:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Transitive via @serverless/util and @serverless/framework. The
          vulnerability is an out-of-range write into a caller-provided `buf`
          passed to uuid v3/v5/v6 (or v4 with a buffer argument). This codebase
          only calls `v4()` with no arguments. The fixed major (uuid@14) drops
          Node.js 18, which the shipped CLI must keep supporting (see
          .github/dependabot.yml).
        expires: 2027-03-10T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-JS-ADMZIP-19276676:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          No fixed version exists. adm-zip is only used to unzip a template
          archive the user explicitly requested by URL (GitHub/GitLab/Bitbucket)
          into a fresh temp directory that is removed afterwards, and by
          `invoke local` for the user's own artifacts. A malicious template
          already yields code execution once deployed, so the symlink-overwrite
          vector adds no meaningful additional exposure.
        expires: 2027-03-10T00:00:00.000Z
